00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:58.060
I didn't have to throw everything out the door just because I didn't believe in the
我并没有因为我不相信某些东西就把一切都全盘否定

151
00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.580
particular religion that I was being asked to practice.
我被要求去信奉的那种特定的宗教。

152
00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:01.780
Yeah.
是的。

153
00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:03.840
That is very powerful.
这真的很有力量。

154
00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.080
That is a real gift.
这真是一个天赋。

155
00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:06.940
And she was like that with all of us.
而且她对我们所有人都这样。

156
00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:07.880
She really cared.
她是真的很关心。

157
00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.720
She didn't treat us like, you know, silly teenagers.
她没有把我们当成那种，你知道的，傻里傻气的青少年。

158
00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.520
She treated us like fully formed, interesting people.
她把我们当成思想成熟、有趣的人。

159
00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.820
So I love her for that.
所以我为此非常爱戴她。

160
00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:17.180
What about you, Ange?
你呢，安吉？

161
00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:22.300
Well, the first teacher that came to mind for me was my theater teacher in elementary
嗯，我脑海中浮现的第一位老师是我小学时的

162
00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:22.700
school.
戏剧老师。

163
00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:25.580
So this was at Jakarta International School.
当时是在雅加达国际学校。

164
00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:30.320
And I had this teacher named Dr. Allen.
我有一位名叫艾伦博士的老师。

165
00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.700
He was an amazing theater director.
他是一位了不起的戏剧导演。

166
00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:36.660
And we would do these fantastic musicals and plays.
我们会排演那些精彩的音乐剧和话剧。

167
00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:42.480
But in his class, it was the first time anyone ever taught me improv.
但在他的课上，那是第一次有人教我即兴表演。

168
00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:50.760
And I was in maybe like fourth grade and he taught us some just very like short form improv games.
当时我大概在上四年级，他教了我们一些非常简短的即兴游戏。

169
00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:54.960
And it was like every single part of my body came alive.
感觉我全身的每个细胞都活了过来。

170
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.440
I was like, what is this?
我当时想，这是什么？

171
00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:58.940
This is the cooleSt.
这太酷了。

172
00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:01.120
I love it so much.
我太喜欢了。

173
00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.920
I want to do this forever.
我想一辈子都做这个。

174
00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:09.000
It was just like electric, you know, because I had seen plays and done school plays and there
那种感觉简直就像触电一样，你知道的，因为我以前看过话剧，也演过学校的话剧，

175
00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.880
was a script and you stuck to the script.
有剧本，而且你得照着剧本演。

176
00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:19.620
But this idea of yes anding and free association and having to really listen and form a scene
但这种“肯定并顺应”（yes and）的理念、自由联想，以及必须真正倾听并与其他人搭档创作一个场景，

177
00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:24.780
with someone else in a partnership was life-changing for me.
对我的生活产生了改变。

178
00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:32.420
And he also took us seriously and was invested and didn't think we were goofballs, but really
而且他也对我们很认真，投入了心血，不觉得我们是在胡闹，而是真心

179
00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:34.860
wanted us to find our own comedic voice.
希望我们能找到属于自己的喜剧之声。

180
00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.960
And I was like, wow.
当时我就想，哇。

181
00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:41.420
I look back in hindsight and I'm like, how amazing to have a teacher like that in elementary.
事后回想起来，我都会感叹，能在小学遇到这样一位老师是多么了不起啊。

182
00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.080
Yeah, that's amazing.
对，这太棒了。

183
00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:48.360
Well, when I was in college, I was a theater major.
嗯，我上大学时主修戏剧。

184
00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:55.320
And I never got the lead roles in anything, in the musicals, in the plays.
我在任何音乐剧或话剧中都从来没有演过主角。

185
00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:59.500
I really had a lot of opportunities in like the student-led productions.
我在学生主导的作品里确实有很多机会。

186
00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.820
We had this lab theater where students would kind of decide.
我们当时有一个实验剧场，由学生们自己做决定。

187
00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:05.960
And like I got to choreograph cabaret and—
我甚至有机会为歌舞剧编排舞蹈，还有——

188
00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.680
Lab theater was like some of my favorite.
实验剧场简直是我最爱的地方之一。

189
00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:08.480
It was great.
太棒了。

190
00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:14.100
Like we had one student who made a musical out of schoolhouse rock cartoons.
比如我们有个学生把“学校屋摇滚”的动画片改编成了音乐剧。

191
00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:16.000
And I got to be in that.
我有幸参演了那个。

192
00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:20.220
So I was always getting cast and being involved in the student lab productions, which honestly
所以我总是能被选中并参与学生的实验剧场作品，说实话，

193
00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:24.940
is really good practice for an actual professional acting career because so much of your professional
这对于真正的职业演艺生涯来说是非常好的锻炼，因为你的职业

194
00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:28.440
acting career is you getting together with your buddies and making stuff.
演艺生涯很大一部分就是和你的死党们聚在一起搞创作。

195
00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:32.980
But in terms of like the mainstream productions, it was harder for me.
但就主流作品而言，对我就比较难了。

196
00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:39.980
But the tech teacher, Ron Rybkowski, he was the person where we had to take classes to
不过技术老师罗恩·雷布科夫斯基（Ron Rybkowski），他要求我们必须上课

197
00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:42.800
learn how to do lights and construction and set design.
学习如何操作灯光、木工制作和布景设计。

198
00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:47.060
He also got to direct one play a year in the summer.
他每年夏天还能执导一部戏。

199
00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:50.980
So if you took the summer session, he was the director of the play.
所以如果你参加了夏季学期的课程，他就是那部戏的导演。

200
00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:57.440
And he gave me a lead role in my last summer session.
他在我最后一个夏季学期里给了我一个主角。

201
00:09:58.120 --> 00:09:59.280
What was it?
是什么剧？

202
00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:01.020
It was Crimes of the Heart.
是《心罪爱满地》。

203
00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:02.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

204
00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:03.860
It's a play about three sisters.
这是一部关于三姐妹的戏剧。

205
00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:10.720
And he cast me as the wild, chain-smoking, bad girl sister.
而他选我演那个狂野、烟不离手、坏女孩的妹妹。

206
00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.500
It was like totally against type.
这完全跟我的形象相反。

207
00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:15.120
But it was so fun.
但真的很有趣。

208
00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:19.500
And it was like the confidence boost that I needed because I was going to graduate then
而且这就像是我需要的自信加持，因为我当时就要毕业了

209
00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:20.660
after that summer session.
在那年暑期课程之后。

210
00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:23.640
And I wanted to be a professional actress and move to Los Angeles.
而且我想成为一名专业演员，搬到洛杉矶去。

211
00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:29.200
And I had gone through my whole four years as a theater major never having a lead role
我读了四年戏剧专业，整个大学期间从来没有在

212
00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:29.820
in a production.
制作中演过主角。

213
00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:32.380
And he finally gave me one.
而他终于给了我一次机会。

214
00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.300
And it really was a boost of confidence.
这真的是一个巨大的自信提升。

215
00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:37.640
But beyond that, he was just always there.
但除此之外，他总是随叫随到。

216
00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:41.120
He was always in his back office if we needed anything.
如果我们有什么需要，他总是在他的后办公室里。

217
00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:47.560
And I remember—this is such a long story—but when I went to jail and I needed someone
我记得——这是一个很长很长的故事——但当我进局子需要人

218
00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:49.140
to bail me out, I called him.
把我保释出来时，我给他打了电话。

219
00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:57.130
It's a very long story, but I had rolled through a stop sign and I got a ticket.
这是一个非常长的故事，但我当时没停车让行，结果吃了一张罚单。

220
00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:59.030
Why'd they take you to jail?
他们为什么把你带进局子？

221
00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:02.510
Because I failed to appear in court for my ticket.
因为我没为那张罚单出庭。

222
00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:02.970
Oh, no.
不会吧。

223
00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:03.490
I forgot.
我给忘了。

224
00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:04.790
It was finals week.
那时正是期末考试周。

225
00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:05.650
I just forgot.
我就是给忘了。

226
00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:06.730
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

227
00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:08.450
I think that happens all the time.
我觉得这种事经常发生。

228
00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:08.870
I know.
我知道。

229
00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:10.830
They put a warrant out for your arreSt.
他们对你发出了逮捕令。

230
00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:17.230
And so two police officers came and knocked on my apartment door, and they arrested me
所以两个警察来敲了我公寓的门，他们把我逮捕了

231
00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:21.110
because I had failed to appear in court for my moving violation.
因为我没有为我的交通违章出庭。

232
00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:22.970
That you forgot about.
就是你忘掉的那张。

233
00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:24.030
That I forgot about.
就是我忘掉的那张。

234
00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:25.510
And I was like, oh, my God.
当时我就想，天哪。

235
00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:26.530
Thank you for reminding me.
谢谢你提醒我。

236
00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:27.230
I'm so sorry.
真的很抱歉。

237
00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:29.570
And they're like, yeah, we're not the reminder police.
他们说，行了，我们可不是提醒警察。

238
00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:31.610
We're like the actual police.
我们是真正的警察。

239
00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:33.470
We're going to have to take you in.
我们得把你带走。

240
00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:38.290
So anyway, I was there, and I was just so embarrassed.
总之，我当时就在那儿，尴尬极了。

241
00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:39.970
And I didn't know who to call.
而且我不知道该打给谁。

242
00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:43.230
I needed a hundred bucks to get bailed out.
我需要一百块钱来保释。

243
00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:44.430
So I called Ron.
所以我给罗恩打了电话。

244
00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:48.410
I called my teacher, Ron Rubkowski, and he came and he bailed me out of jail.
我给我的老师罗恩·鲁布科夫斯基打了电话，他来把我从局子里保释了出去。

245
00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:52.330
And I said, I'm not going to tell my parents.
我说，我打算不告诉我爸妈。

246
00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:54.410
And he said, I think you should.
他说，我觉得你应该告诉他们。

247
00:11:54.470 --> 00:11:58.310
He said, it would break my heart if my daughter didn't share that with me.
他说，如果我的女儿不把这种事跟我分享，我会很心碎的。

248
00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:01.130
He said, I think you can share it with your parents.
他说，我觉得你可以跟你父母说。

249
00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.610
And I'm so glad he told me that because then I did.
我很高兴他当时那样对我说，因为我后来确实说了。

250
00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.150
Do you know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

251
00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:06.410
He was just like a great man.
他就像一个伟大的人。

252
00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:09.870
He's just like a solid, solid person to have in your life.
他就像是你生命中那种真正踏实、可靠的人。

253
00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:11.630
Great advice there for you.
非常棒的建议。

254
00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:12.130
Yes.
是的。

255
00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:12.410
Yeah.
对。

256
00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:19.250
He also took my first headshot for free so that when I went off to Los Angeles, I had
他还免费帮我拍了第一张演员头像，这样我去洛杉矶的时候，

257
00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:19.610
a headshot.
就有头像可用了。

258
00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.290
He did that for every graduating senior.
他为每一届毕业的学长都这样做过。

259
00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:22.330
Amazing.
太惊人了。

260
00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:25.110
So that was a little bit of a meandering story.
所以这个故事有点像是在绕弯子。

261
00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:30.510
But just to say, Harrison, a big thank you to my college professor, Ron Rubkowski.
但我想说的是，哈里森，非常感谢我的大学教授罗恩·鲁布科夫斯基。

262
00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:31.630
All right.
好吧。

263
00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:34.990
Well, my second teacher was my high school English teacher.
那么，我的第二位老师是我的高中英语老师。

264
00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:41.290
And Harrison, I totally related to you saying that for you, it was also your English teacher.
而且哈里森，我对你说的感同身受，对你而言，那也是你的英语老师。

265
00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:42.750
Carol Campbell.
卡罗尔·坎贝尔。

266
00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:45.170
And she taught honors English.
她教的是荣誉英语课。

267
00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:50.430
And she just made stories come to life.
她能让故事变得生动起来。

268
00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.390
And I would have a lot of questions.
我会有很多问题。

269
00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:58.510
And I loved digging into books and seeing if I could make connections or symbolism.
我喜欢深入钻研书本，看看自己能不能找到内在联系或象征意义。

270
00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:01.110
And she was so up for the discussion.
她非常乐意参与讨论。

271
00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:01.910
Do you know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

272
00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:05.770
Like she thought the way my brain worked was really interesting.
就像她觉得我大脑运转的方式非常有趣。

273
00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:09.010
And she encouraged that writer in me.
她鼓励了我心中的那个作家。

274
00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:13.690
My kids right now for their high school English class, Isabel and Jack are reading The Great
我的孩子们现在的高中英语课，伊莎贝尔和杰克正在读《了不起的

275
00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:18.710
Gatsby, and I read The Great Gatsby in Mrs. Campbell's English class.
盖茨比》，而我当年就是在坎贝尔夫人的英语课上读的《了不起的盖茨比》。

276
00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:21.270
Oh, are you so excited for them to read it?
哦，你对他们读这本书感到很兴奋吗？

277
00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:22.590
I'm so excited.
我太兴奋了。

278
00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:23.810
And they're loving it.
而且他们也很喜欢。

279
00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:28.590
And it's been really special because I just remember all the conversations I had with Mrs.
这真的很特别，因为我依稀记得当年我和坎贝尔夫人

280
00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:30.730
Campbell about The Great Gatsby.
关于《了不起的盖茨比》的所有对话。

281
00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:37.990
So yeah, big love to our teachers who are just amazing and there for our kids in so many
所以，是的，向我们的老师们致以大大的爱，他们是那么了不起，在许多方面

282
00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:38.490
ways.
都陪伴着我们的孩子。

283
00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:40.050
Harrison, we loved your question.
哈里森，我们很喜欢你的问题。

284
00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:41.150
Yeah, thank you.
好的，谢谢。

285
00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:43.110
Well, listen, ladies, should we take a break?
听着，女士们，我们要不要休息一下？

286
