我记得我给家人打电话说，我是不是该烤点什么？

445
00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:48.730
Like, what do I need this for?
我留着它能干嘛呢？

446
00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:53.350
It had a huge flat screen TV hooked up to satellite television.
里面有一台连接了卫星电视的超大纯平电视。

447
00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:55.050
It had a fireplace.
它有壁炉。

448
00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:56.910
It had a full bedroom.
它有一间完整的卧室。

449
00:21:57.150 --> 00:21:58.430
It was huge.
它太大了。

450
00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:01.010
I, like, didn't know what to do with myself.
我简直不知道该拿自己怎么办才好了。

451
00:22:01.910 --> 00:22:03.690
Lady, that would have blown my mind.
天哪，那可真让我大开眼界。

452
00:22:03.790 --> 00:22:08.030
I mean, the nicest trailer I've ever had was this past year when we did AT&T.
我是说，我用过最好的化妆车是去年我们拍AT&T广告的时候。

453
00:22:08.270 --> 00:22:10.710
I was like, this trailer is bananas.
当时我都觉得，这车太疯狂了。

454
00:22:10.710 --> 00:22:20.170
But I sort of love that our show was just not like the big Hollywood hullabaloo, you know?
但我其实挺喜欢我们剧组那种不像好莱坞大制作那样大惊小怪的氛围，你知道吗？

455
00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:20.630
Yeah.
对啊。

456
00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:22.630
Because we were all really close because of it.
因为那样我们大家的感情才真的很好。

457
00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:23.750
We weren't spread apart.
我们没有被分散开。

458
00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:28.150
We spent all day on set together in one giant room, basically.
我们基本上整天都在片场的一个超大房间里待在一起。

459
00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:32.450
And then our trailers were all right in this little nook in the parking lot.
而且我们的化妆车都挤在停车场的一个小角落里。

460
00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:33.950
And you had neighbors.
你还有邻居。

461
00:22:33.950 --> 00:22:36.070
You had people right next to you.
旁边就有人。

462
00:22:36.070 --> 00:22:38.750
It was like a little community out there.
外面就像个小社区一样。

463
00:22:38.850 --> 00:22:45.110
And I have to say, because my trailer was so nice on Blades of Glory, I spent a lot of time in it.
我必须得说，因为我在《冰刀双人组》里的化妆车太好了，我在里面呆了很长时间。

464
00:22:45.290 --> 00:22:49.630
Like, I watched that TV when I wasn't needed on set.
比如，片场不需要我的时候，我就在那儿看电视。

465
00:22:49.790 --> 00:22:51.570
I was like, this place is amazing.
当时我就想，这地方太棒了。

466
00:22:51.690 --> 00:22:54.230
This is, like, better than my house.
这简直比我家里还要好。

467
00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:55.230
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

468
00:22:55.730 --> 00:22:57.430
Like, I loved it so much.
真的，我极其喜欢。

469
00:22:57.670 --> 00:23:04.550
And I think, though, because our trailers were not fancy schmancy, we didn't, like, just hang out in them.
不过我想，正因为我们的化妆车没那么豪华，我们才不会总是窝在里面。

470
00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:08.090
And we would play basketball together.
我们会一起打篮球。

471
00:23:08.110 --> 00:23:11.250
Or we would chit-chat and make jokes.
或者我们会闲聊、开玩笑。

472
00:23:11.770 --> 00:23:13.050
Sit on the steps and, like, play music.
坐在台阶上，放放音乐什么的。

473
00:23:13.270 --> 00:23:16.970
We were more social because we didn't have, like, such great digs.
因为住得没那么好，我们反而变得更爱社交了。

474
00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:27.150
I do have a really funny story about, you know, when we were doing The Office, my niece and nephews, they all, at different times, graduated high school.
我确实有一个特别搞笑的故事，你知道的，我们拍《办公室》那会儿，我的侄子和外甥们都在不同的时间高中毕业了。

475
00:23:27.230 --> 00:23:29.210
Because we did the show for nine years, you know?
因为我们拍这部剧拍了九年，你懂的？

476
00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:36.370
And so one of the things I would do is I would fly them out, and they would come to set, and they would get a tour of the set, and they'd have lunch with me on set.
所以我常做的一件事就是机票买好让他们飞过来，他们会来片场参观，然后在片场跟我一起吃午饭。

477
00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:42.670
So my one nephew, he's so sweet, my nephew James, when he came out to visit, I was showing him my trailer.
所以我那个特别贴心的外甥詹姆斯来探班时，我带他参观了我的化妆车。

478
00:23:42.870 --> 00:23:43.750
And here's the thing.
关键是这样的。

479
00:23:43.910 --> 00:23:45.770
We've said our trailers were older, right?
我们刚才说过我们的化妆车比较旧，对吧？

480
00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:46.110
Yeah.
对。

481
00:23:46.110 --> 00:23:46.530
They were older.
确实比较旧。

482
00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:49.350
There was a decorating theme.
里面有一种装修主题。

483
00:23:49.510 --> 00:23:50.490
There was a motif.
有一个母题。

484
00:23:51.050 --> 00:23:52.670
And it was southweSt.
那就是西南风。

485
00:23:53.050 --> 00:23:53.490
Yeah.
没错。

486
00:23:53.690 --> 00:24:04.410
So depending on what trailer you had, there would be kind of like a fakie painting in a wooden frame that was, like, almost like Jim's clown painting in his parents' house.
所以不管你分到哪辆车，里面都会挂着一幅木框的假画，就有点像吉姆父母家里的那幅小丑画。

487
00:24:04.410 --> 00:24:05.990
It was bolted to the wall.
它是用螺栓固定在墙上的。

488
00:24:06.130 --> 00:24:08.310
So, like, there's no moving this picture.
所以，这画根本挪不动。

489
00:24:08.470 --> 00:24:12.870
Whatever trailer you got, there would be a picture, and it would be there no matter what.
不管你分到哪辆车，都会有一幅画，而且它雷打不动地就在那儿。

490
00:24:12.870 --> 00:24:15.910
It was like a wolf, like, howling at the sunset.
就像是一头狼在对著日落长嚎。

491
00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:20.110
Seriously, or like cowboys driving home a cattle range of cows.
真的，或者像牛仔赶着一大群牛在回家的路上。

492
00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:20.510
Yeah.
对。

493
00:24:20.990 --> 00:24:32.590
Or mine was a big sort of clay terracotta pot with, like, etchings on it, like you might see in a cave, you know, of, like, bison or something.
或者我那辆车里是一只巨大的红陶罐，上面有那种你可能在山洞里见过的刻画，比如野牛之类的。

494
00:24:32.710 --> 00:24:33.470
Yes, I remember.
对，我记得。

495
00:24:34.030 --> 00:24:38.630
And my nephew saw it and was like, oh, that's a cool painting.
结果我外甥看到了，就说，哇，这幅画真酷。

496
00:24:38.810 --> 00:24:39.530
That's pretty cool.
挺带劲的嘛。

497
00:24:39.530 --> 00:24:41.630
You brought that and put that out there.
这是你自带并摆在这儿的吧。

498
00:24:41.630 --> 00:24:43.950
You're like, I did not bring, did not bring.
你当时就想说，我可没带，绝对没带。

499
00:24:44.090 --> 00:24:46.510
I was like, oh, honey, it's just here.
我就说，噢，亲爱的，这本来就挂在这儿。

500
00:24:46.650 --> 00:24:47.710
But we did decorate.
不过我们确实装饰过。

501
00:24:48.310 --> 00:24:49.590
We did decorate.
我们确实装饰过了。

502
00:24:49.830 --> 00:24:50.230
We did.
我们确实装饰了。

503
00:24:50.270 --> 00:24:50.970
The girls decorated.
是女孩们装饰的。

504
00:24:51.170 --> 00:24:52.550
The boys didn't really decorate.
男孩们其实没怎么装饰。

505
00:24:52.850 --> 00:24:53.830
The boys did nothing.
男孩们什么都没干。

506
00:24:53.910 --> 00:24:55.890
But, yeah, we decorated a ton.
不过，对，我们装饰得很隆重。

507
00:24:55.970 --> 00:25:00.570
I mean, I had a lamp from home because I love low light.
我是说，我从家里带了一盏灯，因为我喜欢昏暗的灯光。

508
00:25:00.730 --> 00:25:02.950
I'm not a huge fan of, like, overhead fluorescent lights.
我不太喜欢那种头顶上的日光灯。

509
00:25:02.950 --> 00:25:03.230
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

510
00:25:03.370 --> 00:25:06.510
And I would have a plant and I would have a little desk area.
而且我会摆一盆植物，还会有一个小办公桌区域。

511
00:25:06.710 --> 00:25:10.390
Lady, I remember you had made, like, your own little home office nook.
天哪，我记得你弄过自己的小家庭办公角。

512
00:25:10.910 --> 00:25:11.310
Yeah.
对。

513
00:25:11.430 --> 00:25:15.730
I also would bring in a pillow and, like, a nice cozy throw blanket.
我还会带一个枕头和一条舒适的盖毯。

514
00:25:16.170 --> 00:25:17.470
I wanted homey touches.
我想要有家的感觉。

515
00:25:17.830 --> 00:25:18.970
I wanted it to feel cozy.
我想要它感觉很温馨。

516
00:25:19.410 --> 00:25:24.330
But in answer to your question, Emily, at the end of every season, you had to pack everything up.
但回答你的问题，艾米莉，每季结束时，你必须把所有东西都打包好。

517
00:25:24.890 --> 00:25:28.210
Like, these trailers were rented from somewhere.
就像，这些拖车是从某个地方租来的。

518
00:25:28.530 --> 00:25:31.390
And at the end of every season, they get returned.
每季结束时，它们都要被退回。

519
00:25:31.390 --> 00:25:33.170
And then we would get a new set.
然后我们会换上一套新的。

520
00:25:33.950 --> 00:25:35.050
So, yeah.
所以，对。

521
00:25:36.070 --> 00:25:36.390
Yeah.
对。

522
00:25:36.530 --> 00:25:40.070
It was, like, it felt like a college dorm that we had to, like, load in and load out.
这就好像，感觉像大学宿舍一样，我们得把东西搬进搬出。

523
00:25:40.250 --> 00:25:42.270
And that's when the guys would just kind of look at us.
而那时候，男士们就会那样看着我们。

524
00:25:42.350 --> 00:25:44.950
Because on the last day, they would just get in their cars and leave.
因为在最后一天，他们直接上车就走了。

525
00:25:45.330 --> 00:25:45.650
Yeah.
对。

526
00:25:45.670 --> 00:25:47.550
And we would have, like, boxes of things.
而我们却有好多箱东西。

527
00:25:47.610 --> 00:25:49.410
We'd have boxes that we were packing up.
我们得把东西装箱打包。

528
00:25:49.530 --> 00:25:50.790
And we would label things.
我们还会给物品贴标签。

529
00:25:50.930 --> 00:25:55.150
So, it would be, like, trailer bedding, trailer desk stuff.
所以，就会写着，比如，拖车床上用品、拖车办公用品。

530
00:25:55.730 --> 00:25:56.050
Yeah.
对。

531
00:25:56.350 --> 00:26:00.190
And, Angela, you mentioned that our trailers were located in our parking lot.
而且，安吉拉，你提到过我们的拖车就在停车场里。

532
00:26:00.330 --> 00:26:03.390
And they were kind of, like, in a big configuration.
它们是以某种大型阵列摆放的。

533
00:26:03.390 --> 00:26:07.850
And it was a pretty easy walk to get to the stage.
走到片场去非常轻松。

534
00:26:08.690 --> 00:26:16.070
But sometimes when you're on a show or a movie or on a location, your trailers are actually really far away from the set.
但有时当你拍电视剧、电影或者在外景地时，你的拖车其实离片场非常远。

535
00:26:16.070 --> 00:26:20.770
And you have to ride in, like, a van or a golf cart or something to get to the set.
你必须坐面包车、高尔夫球车或者类似的东西才能去片场。

536
00:26:20.970 --> 00:26:24.930
But for us, it was, like, you could walk to the stages.
但对我们来说，就像是，你可以直接走到片场。

537
00:26:25.430 --> 00:26:26.170
You could.
确实可以。

538
00:26:26.310 --> 00:26:27.470
But I do want to share something.
但我确实想分享一件事情。

539
00:26:27.610 --> 00:26:28.570
And I love this lady.
我很喜欢这位女士。

540
00:26:28.570 --> 00:26:29.970
I reached out to Steve Burgess.
我联系了史蒂夫·伯吉斯。

541
00:26:30.110 --> 00:26:31.930
And he sent me some great details I'm going to share in a minute.
他发给我一些很棒的细节，我一会儿就分享。

542
00:26:31.930 --> 00:26:36.290
But he also sent me a ton of pictures of our trailers, just all in a row.
但他还发给我一大堆我们拖车的照片，全排成一排。

543
00:26:36.690 --> 00:26:38.510
And here's the thing I have to share.
事情是这样的，我必须分享一下。

544
00:26:39.570 --> 00:26:44.150
So, you know, when you're cast on a show, on the call sheet, you're numbered.
所以，你知道的，当你参演一部剧时，在通告单上，你是按数字编号的。

545
00:26:44.410 --> 00:26:46.070
And so, Steve was number one.
所以，史蒂夫是一号。

546
00:26:46.210 --> 00:26:46.430
Yes.
是的。

547
00:26:46.450 --> 00:26:49.410
So, his trailer was closest to the stage door.
所以他的拖车离片场大门最近。

548
00:26:49.530 --> 00:26:49.930
Okay.
好吧。

549
00:26:50.050 --> 00:26:51.710
And Steve had a full-size trailer.
而且史蒂夫有一辆标准尺寸的全尺寸拖车。

550
00:26:51.830 --> 00:26:55.890
He was the only one of us who had a full trailer all to himself.
他是我们当中唯一一个独占一整辆大拖车的人。

551
00:26:56.290 --> 00:26:56.630
Yeah.
对。

552
00:26:56.630 --> 00:26:58.850
But he was the closest to the door.
但他离门最近。

553
00:26:58.930 --> 00:26:59.810
Very close to the door.
离门非常近。

554
00:27:00.210 --> 00:27:02.470
So, now, I was number eight.
所以，当时我是八号。

555
00:27:02.690 --> 00:27:05.110
So, I had a little further walk.
所以，我要多走一小段路。

556
00:27:05.250 --> 00:27:06.130
You were down a row.
你在后面一排。

557
00:27:06.150 --> 00:27:06.490
You did.
确实如此。

558
00:27:06.690 --> 00:27:06.990
Yeah.
对。

559
00:27:06.990 --> 00:27:08.150
I was down the row.
我在后一排。

560
00:27:08.330 --> 00:27:12.630
And the supporting cast would kind of, like, joke about that, like, where we were at in the row.
而且配角们有时会开玩笑，比如拿我们在排里的位置开涮。

561
00:27:12.790 --> 00:27:16.630
Well, that was a crazy thing about our show, which was that our trailers were outside.
嗯，我们节目有个很疯狂的地方，那就是我们的化妆车都在外面。

562
00:27:16.790 --> 00:27:20.270
Like, a lot of times, if you're in the fancy studios, you actually don't have trailers.
就像，很多时候，如果你在高级的片场，其实是没有化妆车的。

563
00:27:20.350 --> 00:27:21.350
You have dressing rooMs.
你们有的是化妆间。

564
00:27:21.670 --> 00:27:23.710
And they're, like, attached to your stage.
而且它们就挨着你们的摄影棚。

565
00:27:23.870 --> 00:27:26.210
And so, you're, like, indoors the whole time.
所以，你们全程都在室内。

566
00:27:26.770 --> 00:27:31.990
But our hair and makeup, where we got ready for hair and makeup, was a giant trailer out in the parking lot.
但我们的发型和化妆，我们做造型的地方，是停车场里一个巨大的化妆车。

567
00:27:32.170 --> 00:27:37.070
So, on those rainy days, I remember how frustrated hair and makeup would be, particularly hair.
所以，在那些下雨天，我记得发型和化妆部门会有多沮丧，尤其是发型师。

568
00:27:37.290 --> 00:27:39.290
Because they'd be like, well, I'm going to get you all ready.
因为他们会觉得，好吧，我要给你们把造型全做好。

569
00:27:39.290 --> 00:27:42.330
And now, you're just going to walk in the rain to your trailer and get dressed.
然后呢，你们就要顶着雨走到各自的化妆车去换衣服。

570
00:27:42.450 --> 00:27:45.650
And then, you're going to walk in the rain again to get to the stages.
接着，你们又要顶着雨走去摄影棚。

571
00:27:45.670 --> 00:27:48.270
By the time you get there, I'm just going to have to start all over again.
等你们到那儿的时候，我只能一切从头再来了。

572
00:27:48.270 --> 00:27:49.110
Yes.
是的。

573
00:27:49.430 --> 00:27:52.610
Well, now I want to share with you this email I got from Steve Burgess.
好了，现在我想跟你们分享一封我收到史蒂夫·伯吉斯的邮件。

574
00:27:52.910 --> 00:27:55.130
You know, we trade emails, Jenna and I, and Steve.
你知道的，我们会互相发邮件，珍娜和我，还有史蒂夫。

575
00:27:55.270 --> 00:27:57.950
And he sends us pictures from his life in Tennessee.
他会给我们发他在田纳西州生活的照片。

576
00:27:57.970 --> 00:27:59.550
And we send him pictures back.
我们也会回传照片给他。

577
00:27:59.550 --> 00:28:01.090
He's just the most wonderful person.
他简直是个最好的人。

578
00:28:01.670 --> 00:28:05.410
And so, I was emailing him about Isabel turning 18, you know.
所以，我给他发邮件聊到伊莎贝尔快满18岁的事，你懂的。

579
00:28:06.050 --> 00:28:07.990
And so, we had started this back and forth.
然后我们就这样你来我往地聊了起来。

580
00:28:08.090 --> 00:28:14.210
And I said, hey, while we're chatting, do you have any memories of our base camp and our trailers?
我说，嘿，正好在聊天，你对我们的演员大本营和化妆车有什么回忆吗？

581
00:28:14.210 --> 00:28:17.470
Because we got this really fun fan question, and we're going to talk about it.
因为我们收到了一个非常有趣的粉丝提问，我们要聊聊这个。

582
00:28:17.650 --> 00:28:23.430
And I also asked him, how many trailers at any given time did we have in that parking lot?
我还问他，我们在那个停车场里，任何时候都有多少辆化妆车？

583
00:28:23.650 --> 00:28:25.570
And so, here's some of the stuff he wrote back.
所以，这里有些他回复的内容。

584
00:28:25.590 --> 00:28:25.990
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

585
00:28:26.110 --> 00:28:26.430
I am.
我准备好了。

586
00:28:26.710 --> 00:28:30.510
First of all, he said about our trailers, they weren't a four-star hotel.
首先，关于我们的化妆车，他说，它们可不是四星级酒店。

587
00:28:31.090 --> 00:28:33.650
But they were okay to survive in while not on set.
但不在片场时，在里面凑合度日还行。

588
00:28:33.950 --> 00:28:38.390
By the time I joined the office, it was season six, and everyone was pretty settled in their trailers.
等我加入《办公室》时已经是第六季了，大家都已经在各自的化妆车里安顿下来了。

589
00:28:39.570 --> 00:28:42.710
And then I asked him about what happened when we would go on location.
然后我问他，当我们去外景地时会发生什么。

590
00:28:43.290 --> 00:28:45.490
He said, for the most part, it was manageable.
他说，大体上来说，还是可以应付的。

591
00:28:45.790 --> 00:28:48.550
But other times, our base camp looked like a small city.
但有时，我们的大本营看起来就像一座小城市。

592
00:28:48.790 --> 00:28:53.890
We tried to keep things small when we were just going out for a day or two with only a few cast members.
如果我们只是出去拍一两天，只有几个演员，我们会尽量把规模控制得小一点。

593
00:28:54.110 --> 00:28:59.990
But when the whole cast was on location, we had to bring everyone's trailer, plus trailers for guest stars.
但当全体演员都在外景地时，我们得把每个人的化妆车都拉上，还要加上客串演员的化妆车。

594
00:29:00.170 --> 00:29:04.630
We also had to have a cast trailer for the director, usually one for the writer as well.
我们还得为导演准备一个演员化妆车，通常编剧也得有一个。

595
00:29:04.630 --> 00:29:11.490
And then in addition to the cast trailers, we had to have costume, props, grip, electric, hair, makeup, ADs, catering, and transportation.
除了演员化妆车，我们还得有服装车、道具车、灯光车、电力车、发型车、化妆车、执行导演车、餐饮车和交通车。

596
00:29:12.330 --> 00:29:14.070
So, here is an example.
所以，这里有一个例子。

597
00:29:14.290 --> 00:29:19.530
On the christening episode, we shot at a church in Pasadena with the whole entire caSt.
在洗礼那一集，我们在帕萨迪纳的一座教堂拍摄，全体演员全员出动。

598
00:29:19.870 --> 00:29:21.850
This is what was set up at our base camp.
这就是我们大本营的配置。

599
00:29:22.490 --> 00:29:31.110
Four single trailers, three double-banger trailers, four triple-banger trailers, one honey wagon, a camera truck,
四辆单人化妆车，三辆双隔间化妆车，四辆三隔间化妆车，一辆多功能化妆车，一辆摄影车，

600
00:29:31.110 --> 00:29:36.690
a grip truck, a lightning truck, a set dressing truck, a wardrobe trailer, a hair and makeup trailer, a catering truck,
一辆灯光器材车，一辆电火车，一辆布景车，一辆服装车，一辆发型化妆车，一辆餐饮车，

601
00:29:37.190 --> 00:29:44.270
six vans, seven steak bed trucks, two people boovers, which are 30-person buses, one drivable generator,
六辆面包车，七辆平板卡车，两辆“布弗”巴士（即30座的大巴），一台可移动发电机，

602
00:29:44.570 --> 00:29:50.210
one tractor with a generator because the tractor pulled the wardrobe trailer, which was a 40-foot semi when they were connected,
一台带发电机的拖拉机，因为这台拖拉机牵引着衣帽间拖车，连起来时是一辆40英尺长的半挂车，

603
00:29:50.690 --> 00:29:52.770
one church bus, and Jim's car.
一辆教堂巴士，还有吉姆的车。

604
00:29:53.530 --> 00:29:54.090
Wow.
哇。

605
00:29:54.790 --> 00:29:56.550
That was for the christening episode.
那是为洗礼那一集准备的。

606
00:29:56.710 --> 00:29:57.570
Isn't that unreal?
是不是很不可思议？

607
00:29:58.190 --> 00:29:58.470
Yeah.
是啊。

608
00:29:58.470 --> 00:29:59.190
It's amazing.
太惊人了。

609
00:29:59.470 --> 00:30:00.290
That's amazing.
真是太惊人了。

610
00:30:01.250 --> 00:30:07.430
That's something I didn't know if people knew, which is that, like, the point of the trailers is that if we ever went on location,
有一件事我不知道大家知不知道，就是说，这些拖车的意义在于，如果我们去外景地拍摄，

611
00:30:07.570 --> 00:30:09.130
they would just hitch them up and move them.
他们就会把它们挂上车然后移走。

612
00:30:09.230 --> 00:30:16.330
So, like, my dressing room with all its decor and everything that I liked to keep in it would be over at that church that morning.
所以，那天早上，我的化妆间连同里面的所有装饰以及我喜欢放在里面的东西，都会在那座教堂旁。

613
00:30:16.630 --> 00:30:17.630
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

614
00:30:17.930 --> 00:30:23.390
And he sent pictures from when we did the finale, and our base camp does look like a small city.
他发了我们拍大结局时的照片，我们的基地看起来真的像个小城市。

615
00:30:23.610 --> 00:30:25.890
And it rained, and he sent me a picture.
而且还下雨了，他给我发了一张照片。

616
00:30:26.090 --> 00:30:29.950
It was like a mud hole that we had to, like, wade through to get to the food.
那就像是个泥坑，我们得蹚过去才能吃到东西。

617
00:30:29.950 --> 00:30:31.130
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

618
00:30:31.350 --> 00:30:32.150
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

619
00:30:32.530 --> 00:30:36.270
You know, another question that I think people wonder about a lot, at least people have asked me,
你知道的，我觉得大家经常好奇的另一个问题，至少是大家问过我的问题，

620
00:30:36.390 --> 00:30:40.470
is how much time we spent in our trailers and how private they are.
就是我们在拖车里呆了多长时间，以及它们的私密性如何。

621
00:30:40.710 --> 00:30:42.470
Oh, well, they're not private.
哦，好吧，它们可没什么私密性。

622
00:30:42.870 --> 00:30:45.770
If you share a wall, it's not private, just so you know.
如果你跟别人共用一面墙，那就毫无私密性可言，提醒你一下。

623
00:30:45.770 --> 00:30:52.050
But even if you do have, like, a trailer to yourself, it's still not totally a private space.
但即使你拥有像是一辆属于你自己的单人拖车，它也依然算不上完全私密的空间。

624
00:30:52.190 --> 00:30:56.230
There is always someone knocking on your door, entering your trailer.
总是有人敲你的门，进入你的拖车。

625
00:30:56.590 --> 00:31:02.390
They are constantly delivering new clothes or script pages or memos.
他们不断地送来新衣服、剧本页或备忘录。

626
00:31:03.190 --> 00:31:05.570
If you do share a wall, the walls are thin.
如果你确实共用一面墙，那墙是很薄的。

627
00:31:06.090 --> 00:31:06.570
Yeah.
是啊。

628
00:31:06.730 --> 00:31:09.990
In the first season of The Office, I shared a wall with BJ.
在《办公室》的第一季，我和BJ共用一面墙。

629
00:31:10.370 --> 00:31:13.330
I had a double banger, and he was my trailer mate.
我有一辆双拼拖车，他是我的拖车室友。

630
00:31:13.790 --> 00:31:17.870
John and Rain were paired together, and then BJ and I were paired together.
约翰和雷恩被分到了一起，然后我和BJ被分到了一起。

631
00:31:18.030 --> 00:31:19.950
And BJ would listen to music.
而且BJ会听音乐。

632
00:31:20.570 --> 00:31:28.470
And when we moved, I said I didn't want to share a wall with BJ anymore.
等我们搬地方的时候，我说我不想再跟BJ共用一面墙了。

633
00:31:29.630 --> 00:31:31.470
I kicked him out.
我把他给“踢”走了。

634
00:31:31.610 --> 00:31:34.490
I was like, I don't want to listen to your music.
我说，我不想听你的音乐。

635
00:31:34.490 --> 00:31:35.930
It's so loud.
声音太大了。

636
00:31:36.150 --> 00:31:36.890
It's so loud.
声音太大了。

637
00:31:37.030 --> 00:31:41.670
Here's the other thing I remember about BJ being your neighbor was that I would come in
关于BJ做你邻居，我还记得另一件事，那就是我会进来

638
00:31:41.670 --> 00:31:48.770
and hang out with you, and we could hear him lift the toilet seat to go pee because he would
找你玩，我们能听到他掀起马桶盖去小便的声音，因为他总是

639
00:31:48.770 --> 00:31:51.670
fling it open, and it would whack the wall.
“啪”地一下猛地掀开，会撞到墙上。

640
00:31:51.910 --> 00:31:54.770
And the first time I was in there, when it happened, it startled me.
我第一次在那儿听到这动静时，吓了一跳。

641
00:31:54.870 --> 00:31:56.430
And I was like, what was that noise?
我就问，那是什么声音？

642
00:31:56.550 --> 00:31:59.270
And you said, I think it's when he goes pee.
你说，我想那是他去小便吧。

643
00:32:00.370 --> 00:32:02.250
He flings the lid open.
他把盖子猛地掀开。

644
00:32:02.530 --> 00:32:02.870
Yes.
没错。

645
00:32:03.030 --> 00:32:04.790
He was loud.
他动静很大。

646
00:32:05.610 --> 00:32:06.570
And so—
所以——

647
00:32:06.570 --> 00:32:07.710
We love you, BJ.
我们爱伱，BJ。

648
00:32:07.910 --> 00:32:08.570
We love you.
我们爱你。

649
00:32:08.710 --> 00:32:08.970
We love you, BJ.
我们爱你，BJ。

650
00:32:09.250 --> 00:32:11.090
But you were really loud over there.
但你在那边动静真的太大了。

651
00:32:11.590 --> 00:32:16.330
But, you know, you spent as much time in your trailer as you needed to change your clothes,
不过，你知道的，你在化妆车里待的时间只够换衣服，

652
00:32:16.330 --> 00:32:20.830
or if you weren't in a scene, that's where you might go hang out.
或者如果没有你的戏份，你可能会去那里闲晃。

653
00:32:21.430 --> 00:32:21.690
Yeah.
没错。

654
00:32:21.990 --> 00:32:24.410
And Emily asked us, were we able to pick our neighbors?
艾米莉问过我们，我们能挑选邻居吗？

655
00:32:24.570 --> 00:32:25.730
And the answer to that is no.
而答案是不能。

656
00:32:26.010 --> 00:32:30.650
Well, I didn't get to pick who I wanted as my neighbor, but I was able to pick who I didn't
好吧，我没法挑选我想要谁做邻居，但我大概能挑选我

657
00:32:30.650 --> 00:32:31.550
want, I guess.
不想要谁，我猜。

658
00:32:31.710 --> 00:32:32.090
I did.
我选了。

659
00:32:32.110 --> 00:32:32.990
I guess that's true.
我想也是这样。

660
00:32:33.110 --> 00:32:34.870
Say, please, no more.
拜托，别再说了。

661
00:32:35.790 --> 00:32:38.750
Well, as you all know, Kate Flannery was my first neighbor.
好吧，如大家所知，凯特·弗兰内里是我的第一个邻居。

662
00:32:38.750 --> 00:32:44.570
And then my second neighbor was Phyllis, and she was amazing because she's so quiet.
然后我的第二个邻居是菲莉丝，她太棒了，因为她特别安静。

663
00:32:44.890 --> 00:32:49.890
So if you have to pick someone on the office cast to be your neighbor, I highly recommend
所以如果你必须在《办公室》演员里挑一个人当邻居，我强烈推荐

664
00:32:49.890 --> 00:32:50.310
Phyllis.
菲莉丝。

665
00:32:50.550 --> 00:32:56.750
Also, the trailer next to me, so like my windows faced their windows, was Ed HelMs.
还有，我隔壁的化妆车——也就是我的窗户正对着他们的窗户——是艾德·赫姆斯。

666
00:32:57.010 --> 00:33:01.230
And he would play the banjo, and I would open my window so I could hear him playing
他会弹班卓琴，我会打开窗户听他弹

667
00:33:01.230 --> 00:33:02.910
the banjo, and I loved it.
班卓琴，我超爱这个。

668
00:33:02.910 --> 00:33:07.270
So, lady, Ed's trailer was in between mine and yours.
等等，女士，艾德的化妆车在我和你之间。

669
00:33:07.590 --> 00:33:08.070
Yes.
对。

670
00:33:08.390 --> 00:33:10.610
Because he was also my kind of neighbor.
因为他也算我的邻居。

671
00:33:11.090 --> 00:33:13.630
You know, I didn't share a wall with him, but yes.
你知道的，我没有和他共用一面墙，但是是的。

672
00:33:13.810 --> 00:33:17.290
And I could hear his banjo as well, and I loved it.
我也能听到他的班卓琴声，而且我很喜欢。

673
00:33:17.450 --> 00:33:18.230
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

674
00:33:18.290 --> 00:33:23.370
I loved it so much that sometimes if I had a little bit more downtime and like maybe I
我太喜欢了，有时候如果我有更多一点的空闲时间，比如

675
00:33:23.370 --> 00:33:29.610
would take a little cat nap, I would sort of wake to Ed's banjo playing, and I made it
我想打个盹，我常常会被艾德的班卓琴声吵醒，我甚至把它

676
00:33:29.610 --> 00:33:31.450
my alarm on my cell phone.
设成了手机闹钟。

677
00:33:31.590 --> 00:33:33.410
It's like very nostalgic for me.
这让我感觉非常怀念。

678
00:33:33.510 --> 00:33:35.550
Like, if you're going to wake me up, play the banjo.
就像是在说，如果要叫醒我，就弹班卓琴吧。

679
00:33:35.710 --> 00:33:35.890
Yeah.
对。

680
00:33:35.990 --> 00:33:37.490
And then I don't wake up so grumpy.
这样我醒来时就不会那么暴躁了。

681
00:33:38.030 --> 00:33:39.190
John's trailer was loud.
约翰的化妆车很吵。

682
00:33:39.350 --> 00:33:40.230
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

683
00:33:40.370 --> 00:33:41.790
John's trailer was so loud.
约翰的化妆车太吵了。

684
00:33:42.130 --> 00:33:43.810
I don't know what they did in there.
我不知道他们在里面搞什么鬼。

685
00:33:43.910 --> 00:33:48.270
I think they would just yell at the TV or yell at each other when like the Madden football
我想他们就是在对电视大喊大叫，或者当《麦登橄榄球》

686
00:33:48.270 --> 00:33:49.510
was going nutso.
玩得疯狂时互相大喊大叫。

687
00:33:49.710 --> 00:33:49.970
Yeah.
是的。

688
00:33:49.970 --> 00:33:51.730
And so it would shake.
而且它还会晃动。

689
00:33:51.970 --> 00:33:55.710
You would walk by John's trailer, and it would be moving, and it'd be because like
你路过约翰的化妆车时，它甚至在动，那是因为

690
00:33:56.450 --> 00:33:59.990
Brian Baumgartner was like, you know, jumping up and down or something.
布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳在里面，你知道的，上蹿下跳之类的。

691
00:34:00.190 --> 00:34:00.610
Yes, they would.
没错，他们会的。

692
00:34:00.730 --> 00:34:01.590
They would jump up and down.
他们会跳上跳下。

693
00:34:01.670 --> 00:34:04.570
And sometimes we would go in there, and we would just sit and hang out.
有时候我们会进去，然后就坐在那儿闲晃。

694
00:34:04.710 --> 00:34:05.490
And watch them.
看着他们。

695
00:34:05.670 --> 00:34:05.990
Yeah.
对。

696
00:34:06.270 --> 00:34:07.750
If we were like really bored.
如果我们实在无聊的话。

697
00:34:08.330 --> 00:34:11.230
If we were really bored, we'd say, let's go see what the boys are doing.
如果我们真的很无聊，就会说，去看看这帮小子在干嘛吧。

698
00:34:11.490 --> 00:34:11.790
Exactly.
没错。

699
00:34:11.790 --> 00:34:14.230
And they were just yelling at each other and the TV.
而他们只是在对彼此和电视大喊大叫。

700
00:34:14.470 --> 00:34:17.990
And you could hear them walking through the parking lot like, what the hell?
你能听到他们走过停车场时说，搞什么鬼？

701
00:34:18.150 --> 00:34:19.090
Come on, man.
拜托，老兄。

702
00:34:19.450 --> 00:34:19.810
Yes.
对。

703
00:34:19.970 --> 00:34:27.330
But lady, we have to share that when we had kids, we graduated to a very special trailer
但是大姐，我们得承认，当我们有了孩子之后，我们就升级到了一种非常特殊的拖车

704
00:34:27.330 --> 00:34:28.090
configuration.
配置。

705
00:34:28.430 --> 00:34:31.150
This was a time when you really led the way.
那时候你真的是带头人。

706
00:34:31.490 --> 00:34:36.250
They were so wonderful for you when you brought Isabel back after our hiatus.
在我们暂停休息后，你把伊莎贝尔带回来时，他们对你真的太好了。

707
00:34:36.690 --> 00:34:41.950
So I had Isabel right after Goodbye, Toby, because I was super pregnant.
所以我拍完《再见，托比》后不久就生下了伊莎贝尔，因为我当时超级显怀。

708
00:34:42.350 --> 00:34:43.970
They couldn't even hide my belly anymore.
他们甚至再也藏不住我的肚子了。

709
00:34:43.970 --> 00:34:47.650
If you watch that episode when Andy proposes to Angela, you can just see my belly.
如果你看安迪向安吉拉求婚的那集，你一眼就能看到我的肚子。

710
00:34:47.790 --> 00:34:47.930
They gave up.
他们放弃了。

711
00:34:47.930 --> 00:34:49.130
Because they gave up.
因为他们放弃了。

712
00:34:49.330 --> 00:34:52.410
And I had her like, what, lady, like eight days later?
而且我生下她大概是在……天哪，大概八天之后？

713
00:34:52.610 --> 00:34:52.750
Yeah.
对。

714
00:34:52.890 --> 00:34:53.310
Something crazy.
简直疯狂。

715
00:34:53.790 --> 00:34:59.950
And so when I came back to set for season five, I had this newborn.
所以当我回到第五季的片场时，我已经有了这个刚出生的宝宝。

716
00:35:00.050 --> 00:35:04.110
And at first, I would just have her in the trailer with me.
一开始，我只是把她留在我的拖车里。

717
00:35:04.250 --> 00:35:09.350
But like you said, so many people knock throughout the day that I would just kind of be putting
但就像你说的，一天下来有那么多人敲门，我本来刚好在

718
00:35:09.350 --> 00:35:10.250
her down for a nap.
哄她睡午觉。

719
00:35:10.250 --> 00:35:11.610
And I'd have a break at lunch.
我午休的时候本该休息一下。

720
00:35:11.730 --> 00:35:13.230
And I was going to have that cozy time with her.
我本打算和她度过一段温馨的时光。

721
00:35:13.310 --> 00:35:14.550
And someone would knock on the door, right?
结果就会有人敲门，对吧？

722
00:35:14.550 --> 00:35:14.690
Yeah.
对。

723
00:35:14.750 --> 00:35:15.330
And she'd wake up.
然后她就醒了。

724
00:35:15.330 --> 00:35:18.490
So I remember having this conversation with Randy Cordray.
所以我记得我和兰迪·科德雷有过这样一次谈话。

725
00:35:18.670 --> 00:35:19.710
He was so sweet.
他人真的很好。

726
00:35:19.950 --> 00:35:20.830
He was our producer.
他是我们的制片人。

727
00:35:20.830 --> 00:35:24.250
And he was like, Angela, is there anything you need for the baby?
他当时说，安吉拉，你有什么需要给宝宝的吗？

728
00:35:24.470 --> 00:35:25.150
How's it going?
最近怎么样？

729
00:35:25.330 --> 00:35:26.950
You know, being back at work with her.
你知道的，带着她回到工作岗位感觉如何。

730
00:35:27.370 --> 00:35:28.410
What would be helpful?
