And there are down days.
总有低谷的日子。

1023
00:49:32.780 --> 00:49:38.500
I mean, I can think of a few examples when I had to go to work or I had to go on set and I had to film a
我的意思是，我能想到一些例子，当时我不得不去工作，或者不得不去片场，我不得不去拍

1024
00:49:38.500 --> 00:49:41.900
comedy television show and I wasn't in a great mood.
一部喜剧电视剧，而我当时心情并不是很好。

1025
00:49:41.960 --> 00:49:45.140
My grandmother passed away while we were shooting the show.
我外祖母在我们拍摄这部剧的时候去世了。

1026
00:49:45.140 --> 00:49:50.420
And I got that news while I was at work and that was hard.
我在工作时收到了这个消息，这很难受。

1027
00:49:50.660 --> 00:49:56.040
It was hard to just go sit in laughter after that for the rest of that day.
在那之后的那天剩下的时间里，要继续坐在那里欢笑，真的很艰难。

1028
00:49:56.380 --> 00:49:56.540
Yeah.
是的。

1029
00:49:56.700 --> 00:50:02.860
I remember being very thankful in particular for our cast and how much we were there for each other
我记得特别感谢我们的演员阵容，以及我们彼此之间是多么地支持对方，

1030
00:50:02.860 --> 00:50:05.420
because we all had times, you know, like that.
因为我们所有人都有过那种时候，你知道的。

1031
00:50:05.420 --> 00:50:10.320
And I think on some sets you might not have that kind of support in the way that we had.
我想在某些片场，你可能不会拥有我们那种支持。

1032
00:50:10.600 --> 00:50:16.080
But in the early season of the office, early in season two, my mom was very sick and she was in the
但在《办公室》的早期，第二季刚开始的时候，我妈妈病得很重，她在

1033
00:50:16.080 --> 00:50:18.580
hospital and things were touch and go.
医院里，情况非常危急。

1034
00:50:18.780 --> 00:50:20.640
She ended up, you know, pulling through.
她最后，你知道的，挺过来了。

1035
00:50:20.780 --> 00:50:21.960
But it was very scary.
但那真的很吓人。

1036
00:50:21.960 --> 00:50:26.160
And I just remember you and Kate just rallying around me.
我只记得你和凯特一直在周围支持我。

1037
00:50:26.460 --> 00:50:27.100
And you do.
确实如此。

1038
00:50:27.320 --> 00:50:32.700
You have to just kind of dig deep inside yourself and do your job, you know.
你必须从内心深处挖掘力量，把工作做好，你知道的。

1039
00:50:32.920 --> 00:50:36.360
And those are the days where it is just kind of a job, you know.
而且有些日子，它真的就只是一份工作，你知道的。

1040
00:50:36.720 --> 00:50:40.040
But also, Layla, the part of your question where you said,
不过，莱拉，你问题中的那一部分，你提到

1041
00:50:40.140 --> 00:50:42.420
does sometimes, does it actually cheer you up?
有时候，它真的能让你高兴起来吗？

1042
00:50:42.800 --> 00:50:49.260
There had been mornings where nothing in particular bad or anything scary was happening.
曾经有过这样的早晨，并没有发生什么特别糟糕或可怕的事情。

1043
00:50:49.260 --> 00:50:54.960
But maybe you just had a frazzled morning getting out the door and you're just in that kind of mood
但也许你出门时手忙脚乱，你就是那种心情，

1044
00:50:54.960 --> 00:50:58.120
where you walk onto set and you're just like, well, okay, now what?
当你走进片场时，你就会想，好吧，现在又怎么了？

1045
00:50:58.340 --> 00:51:05.180
And then we would have a scene and Steve Carell as Michael would do that laugh that he does
然后我们会有一场戏，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔饰演的迈克尔会发出那种他标志性的笑声，

1046
00:51:05.180 --> 00:51:07.380
when he acts, his acting laugh.
他演戏时的笑声。

1047
00:51:07.580 --> 00:51:09.280
And it's so damn funny.
而且太该死的好笑了。

1048
00:51:09.480 --> 00:51:14.480
I would find myself laughing or trying not to laugh because my character could never really
我会发现自己笑出来，或者极力克制不笑，因为我的角色永远不能真正

1049
00:51:14.480 --> 00:51:15.540
bust out laughing.
放声大笑。

1050
00:51:15.540 --> 00:51:20.720
But there were so many times when Steve pretending to laugh cheered me up.
但有太多次，史蒂夫假装大笑让我开心了起来。

1051
00:51:21.160 --> 00:51:22.000
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1052
00:51:22.300 --> 00:51:27.700
I mean, I think overall, it was such a beneficial place to work.
我是说，我觉得总体而言，这是一个非常棒的工作场所。

1053
00:51:27.700 --> 00:51:35.640
To go into a place where your job was being around comedy and making comedy, it did affect my mood.
去一个以喜剧和创作喜剧为工作的地方，这确实影响了我的心情。

1054
00:51:35.840 --> 00:51:42.480
And I remember I would think, gosh, I often leave work in a happier mood than when I got there
我记得我曾想过，天哪，我下班时的心情往往比上班时还要好，

1055
00:51:42.480 --> 00:51:45.220
just by virtue of having laughed all day.
仅仅因为整天都在欢笑。

1056
00:51:45.580 --> 00:51:51.760
And I thought, what's it like to play a character on a drama where you're dealing with like intense
我想，在正剧里扮演一个整天都要面对紧张题材、

1057
00:51:51.760 --> 00:51:56.560
subject matter all day or you have to cry all day or you have to have like an intense scene?
或者整天都要哭泣、或者必须演紧张戏份的角色，会是什么感觉？

1058
00:51:56.700 --> 00:51:59.760
Because that gets into the fiber of you, you know?
因为那些东西会融入你的骨髓，你知道吗？

1059
00:51:59.860 --> 00:52:05.120
It's like it's pretend, but you are accessing things in order to bring it forward.
这就像是假装的，但为了呈现出来，你必须调动内心的感受。

1060
00:52:05.460 --> 00:52:09.640
Or exposing yourself to things if it's like subject matter that's really troubling.
或者让自己接触那些真正令人烦恼的题材。

1061
00:52:09.640 --> 00:52:11.280
Yes, yes.
没错，没错。

1062
00:52:11.540 --> 00:52:11.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1063
00:52:11.900 --> 00:52:12.480
It's funny.
这很有趣。

1064
00:52:12.580 --> 00:52:19.600
When we did our rewatch, you know that episode where Pam and Jim, they go to buy stuff to cheer
当我们重温剧集时，你知道那一集吗？帕姆和吉姆去买东西来让凯文开心，

1065
00:52:19.600 --> 00:52:20.040
up Kevin.
那是迈克尔的生日。

1066
00:52:20.140 --> 00:52:21.140
It's Michael's birthday.
但所有人都很担心凯文。

1067
00:52:21.380 --> 00:52:23.060
But everyone's worried about Kevin.
所有人都很担心凯文。

1068
00:52:23.240 --> 00:52:24.140
Everyone's worried about Kevin.
然后帕姆有个小桥段，她模仿说，卢克，我是你父亲。

1069
00:52:24.360 --> 00:52:29.160
And Pam has her little thing where she's like, Luke, I am your father.
她演了整段。

1070
00:52:29.460 --> 00:52:30.620
She does the whole thing.
她演了整段。

1071
00:52:31.140 --> 00:52:39.720
So that day that we filmed in that store, I won't share why, but I was pretty down that day.
所以那天我们在那家店里拍戏时，原因我就不分享了，但我那天情绪挺低落的。

1072
00:52:40.180 --> 00:52:41.960
I wasn't in a good mood.
我心情不太好。

1073
00:52:41.960 --> 00:52:46.040
And I remembered worrying that you might see it in my performance.
我记得当时还担心你可能会从我的表演中看出这一点。

1074
00:52:46.280 --> 00:52:49.820
And when we did the rewatch, I thought, no, I think if I didn't know, I would know.
而当我们重温那一集时，我想，不，我觉得如果我不知道内情，我大概也看不出来。

1075
00:52:50.260 --> 00:52:54.640
But for whatever reason, that was a tough one that day to go in.
但不管怎样，那天去上班确实挺不容易的。

1076
00:52:54.640 --> 00:52:56.580
Because I had to be funny.
因为我必须表现得搞笑。

1077
00:52:56.960 --> 00:53:00.660
Like, I had to be peppy and up and flirty and funny.
我是说，我必须表现得有活力、积极、调皮又好笑。

1078
00:53:00.660 --> 00:53:02.380
And I was not feeling it.
而我当时根本没有那种状态。

1079
00:53:02.760 --> 00:53:04.200
But I think I covered.
不过我想我掩饰过去了。

1080
00:53:04.860 --> 00:53:05.980
I think you did.
我想你确实做到了。

1081
00:53:06.220 --> 00:53:07.360
I think you did fantastic.
我觉得你表现得棒极了。

1082
00:53:07.800 --> 00:53:08.060
Yeah.
对。

1083
00:53:08.180 --> 00:53:13.420
I think the hardest thing for me, Layla, was the reverse, which is playing a grump around
莱拉，对我来说最难的事情其实恰恰相反，就是在那么多搞笑的人周围扮演一个脾气暴躁的人。

1084
00:53:13.420 --> 00:53:15.140
a lot of really funny people.
因为我也想笑。

1085
00:53:16.580 --> 00:53:18.000
Because I wanted to laugh.
而且我确实在笑。

1086
00:53:18.000 --> 00:53:19.000
And I was laughing.
我一直在努力克制不让自己笑出来。

1087
00:53:19.020 --> 00:53:22.080
And I was trying to suppress laughter all the time.
而且，詹娜，你知道的，说到这样一份工作：有时你带着许多心事去上班，

1088
00:53:22.080 --> 00:53:28.060
And, you know, I will say, Jenna, talk about a job where sometimes you come to work and
但一天工作结束时，你却带着更快乐的心情离开。

1089
00:53:28.060 --> 00:53:32.560
you've just got a lot going on, but then you leave at the end of your workday happier.
我和你还有我们的播客也是这样。

1090
00:53:32.560 --> 00:53:35.460
And that is true for me with you and our podcaSt.
哦，确实。

1091
00:53:35.900 --> 00:53:36.760
Oh, yeah.
是啊。

1092
00:53:36.860 --> 00:53:37.120
Yeah.
很多时候我们录制结束，特别是我们在录音室的时候，一录完，

1093
00:53:37.500 --> 00:53:43.180
So many times when we're done recording, especially when we're in studio, the minute we're done,
我们就一起走到停车场。

1094
00:53:43.320 --> 00:53:44.600
we walk to our cars together.
一路上我们都在聊天。

1095
00:53:44.900 --> 00:53:46.680
We talk the whole entire way.
我们会在其中一辆车旁站着聊个不停。

1096
00:53:46.880 --> 00:53:51.900
We have a whole chat session, like standing next to one of our cars.
然后我们上车开车回家，

1097
00:53:52.080 --> 00:53:56.800
And then we get in our cars and we drive home and we either leave each other a message
在开回家的路上，要么给对方留语音，

1098
00:53:56.800 --> 00:53:58.700
or call each other on the drive home.
要么给对方打电话。

1099
00:53:58.900 --> 00:54:01.020
I mean, it's just like being back on the set.
我的意思是，这感觉就像回到了片场一样。

1100
00:54:01.300 --> 00:54:02.040
I know.
我知道。

1101
00:54:02.240 --> 00:54:02.780
I know.
我知道。

1102
00:54:03.060 --> 00:54:04.260
So I love it.
所以我很喜欢。

1103
00:54:04.380 --> 00:54:06.200
I love doing this podcast with you, lady.
我也很喜欢跟你一起做这个播客，老姐。

1104
00:54:06.900 --> 00:54:07.360
Thanks.
谢谢。

1105
00:54:07.860 --> 00:54:08.400
Me too.
我也是。

1106
00:54:08.940 --> 00:54:09.220
Aw.
噢。

1107
00:54:09.500 --> 00:54:11.560
Well, you guys, thank you so much.
好了，各位，非常感谢。

1108
00:54:11.700 --> 00:54:13.740
This was a fun trip down memory lane for us.
对我们来说，这是一次充满回忆的趣味之旅。

1109
